          "content": "Begin with the following problem: A system description supplies A\u2192B and A. A correct derivation obtains B by implication elimination; it does not infer A from B without an additional premise. Write the problem in ordinary language first. Identify which words introduce conjunctions, alternatives, negations, quantifiers, or claims of necessity. Then separate object-level statements from the evaluator's assumptions. State a proposed formalization and one plausible alternative. For each, ask what observation or interpretation would distinguish them. Finally, explain which parts can be checked by logic alone and which require additional factual or policy evidence. A correct formal answer must be precise enough for another student to reproduce without guessing the intended meanings.",
